  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aquaculture Working Group</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is closely related to other activities in the aquaculture sector undertaken by RVO and the Netherlands Embassies (EKNs) of Tanzania and Kenya. In 2013, FoodTech Africa-Kenya was created through the FDOV programme, which is still operational. Since the beginning of 2018, the lessons learned in Kenya have expanded to Tanzania within the impact cluster Aquaculture. The working group meetings facilitated by this project are of utmost importance for the success and impact of the impact cluster. The project is implemented, in close collaboration with FoodtechAfrica, from 1 October 2019 to 31 December 2020.Objective:The working group intends to create a platform (Public and Private) for cooperation between Tanzania and the Netherlands in addressing issues that could facilitate and enable the environment for aquaculture sector development. It has been agreed upon in the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) signed between the Netherlands and the Tanzanian government.Updated information, knowledge and sector progress will trigger actions to be taken by the authorities. It also supports the FoodTechAfrica impact cluster to understand recent developments and allow airing out issues that could be challenging at that particular time.As the stakeholders in Tanzania are located in different locations, the working groups are expensive to organize. This PSD Toolkit project has been developed to enable the Dutch Embassy to invite the working group members to meet at least three times during the remainder of the Impact Cluster. In the long term, this project will create an enabling environment for the further development of the aquaculture sector and private sector investments within the aquaculture value chain in Tanzania. At the same time, it aligns with the Tanzanian national industrialization agenda.</narrative>
  </description>
